---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
---

<Base
  title="Join us"
  description="Opportunities for graduate students, visiting researchers, and industry partners at the SMI Lab."
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="Opportunities"
    title="Join us"
    lead="We are looking for people who want to understand how marine structures behave — and who care about getting the answer right."
  />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
      <h2>Graduate students</h2>
      <p>
        We supervise MSc and PhD students in the Department of Naval Architecture and Ocean
        Engineering. A background in naval architecture, ocean, civil, mechanical, or
        aerospace engineering is a natural fit, as is any strong grounding in solid mechanics
        and numerical methods.
      </p>
      <p>
        Students in the lab work across mechanics-based structural assessment, offshore
        renewable energy structures, and the digital methods that connect them. Prior
        experience with finite element analysis or programming is useful, but curiosity and
        rigour matter more.
      </p>

      <h2>Visiting researchers</h2>
      <p>
        We host visiting researchers and exchange students for defined periods of joint work.
        Please write with your research interests, the period you have in mind, and any
        funding you already hold.
      </p>

      <h2>Industry collaboration</h2>
      <p>
        We work with shipyards, operators, classification societies, and technology developers
        on structural integrity, fatigue and fracture assessment, offshore wind structures, and
        alternative fuel containment. Collaboration ranges from focused technical studies to
        multi-year funded projects.
      </p>

      <h2>How to get in touch</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> with a short description of
        your interests. For graduate applications, please include:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>A CV, including your academic record</li>
        <li>A brief statement of the research problems that interest you and why</li>
        <li>Your intended start date and funding situation, if known</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="note">
        Applications to the graduate programme are handled through Inha University's central
        admissions process. Contacting us beforehand is welcome and helps us tell you whether
        there is a good match.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .note {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--c-accent);
    background: var(--c-bg-subtle);
    padding: 0.9rem 1.1rem;
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius) var(--radius) 0;
    font-size: 0.94rem;
  }
</style>
